Hi, great project here. Since the latest Version of VS Code, we can now use the MCP in Copilot. I managed to get it working with our Jira. I can requests Jira-Issue in Copilot. That is soo nice.

But I cannot create an issue. I always run into the error ``Error: Component is required``.

Manually I can create an issue like this:

```bash
POST {{jiraUrl}}/rest/api/2/issue
Authorization: Basic {{jiraUsername}}:{{jiraApiToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
```

With this body:

```json
{
  "fields": {
    "project": {
      "key": "MyKey"
    },
    "summary": "Test Issue via HTTP Client",
    "description": "This is a Test-Issue",
    "issuetype": {
      "name": "Story"
    },
    "components": [
      {
        "name": "Long Name of the component"
      }
    ],
    "customfield_10041": "MyStringValue"
  }
}
```

I assume, that the components are not handled like the other custom fields in the api.
